  <metadata minClientVersion="2.12">
    <id>MimeKit.Cryptography</id>
    <version>5.0.0</version>
    <title>MimeKit.Cryptography</title>
    <authors>Jeffrey Stedfast</authors>
    <owners>Jeffrey Stedfast</owners>
    <license type="expression">MIT</license>
    <projectUrl>https://www.mimekit.net</projectUrl>
    <repository type="git" url="https://github.com/jstedfast/MimeKit" />
    <icon>icons\mimekit-50.png</icon>
    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <description>
      MimeKit is an Open Source library for creating and parsing MIME, S/MIME and PGP messages on desktop and mobile platforms. It also supports parsing of Unix mbox files.

      MimeKit.Cryptography extends MimeKit.Core with support for S/MIME, PGP/MIME, DKIM, ARC and DMARC using BouncyCastle.Cryptography. Reference this package (or the MimeKit meta-package) when you need cryptography features.

      API documentation can be found on the web at http://www.mimekit.net/docs

      For those that need SMTP, POP3 or IMAP support, check out https://github.com/jstedfast/MailKit
    </description>
    <summary>An Open Source library for creating and parsing MIME, S/MIME and PGP messages on desktop and mobile platforms.</summary>
    <releaseNotes>
MimeKit 5.0 is a major release containing a number of breaking changes. See https://github.com/jstedfast/MimeKit/blob/master/ReleaseNotes.md for the complete list of changes and migration notes.

* MimeKit.Cryptography contains the S/MIME, PGP/MIME, DKIM, ARC and DMARC support that was previously part of MimeKit. Call CryptographyModule.Initialize () during startup, and add a using MimeKit.Cryptography; directive for the MimeMessage.Sign (), Encrypt () and SignAndEncrypt () extension methods.
* Visitors that handle signed or encrypted entities must now derive from CryptographicMimeVisitor.
* CryptographyContext no longer registers a default S/MIME context. Applications must explicitly register the context they want. This makes MimeKit AOT-compatible.
* Added DmarcVerifier and DmarcRecord for DMARC validation.
* Replaced IDkimPublicKeyLocator with the more general IDnsResolver interface, and DKIM key records are now parsed more strictly per RFC 6376.
* DkimVerifier.Verify () now returns a DkimSignatureValidationResult describing why a signature did not pass, and ArcVerifier.Verify () now provides diagnostics for ARC chain validation failures.
* MimeMessage.Sign () and SignAndEncrypt () overloads that do not take a DigestAlgorithm now use SHA-256 instead of SHA-1.
* Moved the digest algorithm preference APIs from CryptographyContext to OpenPgpContext.
* Removed previously obsoleted APIs, including the obsolete DkimSigner, ArcSigner and IX509CertificateDatabase APIs.
    </releaseNotes>
    <copyright>.NET Foundation and Contributors</copyright>
    <language>en-US</language>
    <tags>mime encryption arc dkim dmarc security smime s/mime openpgp pgp mbox mail email parser tnef</tags>
    <readme>docs\README.md</readme>
